==English==
{{was wotd|2007|June|19}}

===Etymology===
{{PIE root|en|swep}}
First attested in 1615. {{bor|en|fr|somnolent}}, from {{der|en|fro|sompnolent}}, subsequently from {{der|en|la|somnolentus}}, from {{m|la|somnus||sleep}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*swépnos}}, {{m|ine-pro|*súpnos||dream}}, which both are derived from {{etyl|ine-pro|en}} {{m|ine-pro|*swep-}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|RP}} {{IPA|/ˈsɒmnələnt/|lang=en}}
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|/ˈsɑːmnələnt/|lang=en}}
* {{audio|en-us-somnolent.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# [[drowsy|Drowsy]] or [[sleepy]].
# {{lb|en|dated}} Causing literal or figurative sleepiness; [[soporific]].

